    {
      "id": "E9GrnbOxQ05KNs_A4CbWl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4906.031746031743,
      "y": -1979.988095238095,
      "width": 2062.466666666664,
      "height": 1529.9999999999989,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1013022340,
      "version": 1289,
      "versionNonce": 438921350,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "yyfv2L5AojZOWpPZGyi0G",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1788593385753,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A runtime structure that keeps track of everything JavaScript needs while executing a particular piece of code.\n\nThere are mainly 3 types :- \n\n1. Global Execution Context :- Created when your JavaScript program starts.\n2. Function Execution Context :- Created every time a function is called.\n3. Eval Execution Context :- Created when eval() executes code. You generally won't use eval(), so don't worry about\nthis one for now.\n\nHow it look like :-\n \nGlobal Execution Context\n├── x -> variable\n├── add -> function\n\nFunction Execution Context\n├── a = 5\n├── b = 3\n├── result = 8\n\nThink :- \"Where/how this code is currently executing\"\n\n\"Where\" refers to the scope and environment the code sit like when we create a variable globally i can be accessable\nby everyone but Code running inside a specific function. It has its own private workspace containing its parameters\nand locally declared variables.\n\n\"How\" refers to the rules, mechanisms, and internal setup applied to run that code. for e.g.\nHow the code determines what this points to , \nIt do Hoisting means it parse the code text to find keywords like var, let, const, and function and reserve memory\nfor them :- \n     -  Thats why when you call a function before creating it. it works fines because all declarations were magically\n\"hoisted\" (pulled) to the very top of the file or function.\n     - when you call the var vraiuable before creating it. it give undefined\n     - when call let / const before creating give Throws a ReferenceError if accessed",
      "fontSize": 35.99999999999997,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A runtime structure that keeps track of everything JavaScript needs while executing a particular piece of code.\n\nThere are mainly 3 types :- \n\n1. Global Execution Context :- Created when your JavaScript program starts.\n2. Function Execution Context :- Created every time a function is called.\n3. Eval Execution Context :- Created when eval() executes code. You generally won't use eval(), so don't worry about this one for now.\n\nHow it look like :-\n \nGlobal Execution Context\n├── x -> variable\n├── add -> function\n\nFunction Execution Context\n├── a = 5\n├── b = 3\n├── result = 8\n\nThink :- \"Where/how this code is currently executing\"\n\n\"Where\" refers to the scope and environment the code sit like when we create a variable globally i can be accessable by everyone but Code running inside a specific function. It has its own private workspace containing its parameters and locally declared variables.\n\n\"How\" refers to the rules, mechanisms, and internal setup applied to run that code. for e.g.\nHow the code determines what this points to , \nIt do Hoisting means it parse the code text to find keywords like var, let, const, and function and reserve memory for them :- \n     -  Thats why when you call a function before creating it. it works fines because all declarations were magically \"hoisted\" (pulled) to the very top of the file or function.\n     - when you call the var vraiuable before creating it. it give undefined\n     - when call let / const before creating give Throws a ReferenceError if accessed",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c8snNs9dgLIuhnCmaEK06",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4924.762486772484,
      "y": 93.01190476190527,
      "width": 2051.005185185182,
      "height": 318.4999999999996,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 877818044,
      "version": 1648,
      "versionNonce": 477215548,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788363574222,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every time a function is called, JavaScript creates a function execution context.\nWhere does JavaScript keep track of those execution contexts while they are running? That's where the Call Stack\ncomes in. ( Last In, First Out )\n\nJavaScript is generally single-threaded.\nImp :- Meaning, one JavaScript execution thread has one call stack and can execute one piece of JavaScript at a\ntime. as it runs line by line",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every time a function is called, JavaScript creates a function execution context.\nWhere does JavaScript keep track of those execution contexts while they are running? That's where the Call Stack comes in. ( Last In, First Out )\n\nJavaScript is generally single-threaded.\nImp :- Meaning, one JavaScript execution thread has one call stack and can execute one piece of JavaScript at a time. as it runs line by line",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "q1nwnTctczQ44-ty7vaFR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10384.762486772484,
      "y": -2116.9880952380945,
      "width": 1327.5414781571471,
      "height": 363.99999999999955,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2018862704,
      "version": 1817,
      "versionNonce": 2072048736,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788544561885,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Web APIs are features provided by the browser, not by JavaScript itself.\"\n\nDon't think:\"Web API = asynchronous.\"That's not necessarily true.\ndocument.querySelector(\"#box\");\nDOM APIs are Web APIs, but this operation is synchronous.\n\nSome Web APIs involve asynchronous operations, and those operations\neventually interact with Tasks/Microtasks.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Web APIs are features provided by the browser, not by JavaScript itself.\"\n\nDon't think:\"Web API = asynchronous.\"That's not necessarily true.\ndocument.querySelector(\"#box\");\nDOM APIs are Web APIs, but this operation is synchronous.\n\nSome Web APIs involve asynchronous operations, and those operations eventually interact with Tasks/Microtasks.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WD_0DyUtJXFX9k84bFHxW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10381.128905366882,
      "y": -951.3020471415421,
      "width": 1327.5414781571471,
      "height": 818.999999999999,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1977893008,
      "version": 2409,
      "versionNonce": 376711792,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788454328650,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now Js start execution first it send log to the stack and print the\noutput then there is turn of setTimeout as it is a webAPI now this tell\nto browser \"Start a timer for this callback\". and js do not wait here it\ncontinues and print the c\nNow setTimeout do not directly go into the call stack when the 0ms get\nexpried the browser say \"Okay, this callback is now ready to run.\" and It\nputs the callback into the Task Queue.\nNow here the Event loop comes it continously asking :- \n\nIs the Call Stack empty?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nIs there a task waiting in the Task Queue?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nMove that task to the Call Stack",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now Js start execution first it send log to the stack and print the output then there is turn of setTimeout as it is a webAPI now this tell to browser \"Start a timer for this callback\". and js do not wait here it continues and print the c\nNow setTimeout do not directly go into the call stack when the 0ms get expried the browser say \"Okay, this callback is now ready to run.\" and It puts the callback into the Task Queue.\nNow here the Event loop comes it continously asking :- \n\nIs the Call Stack empty?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nIs there a task waiting in the Task Queue?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nMove that task to the Call Stack",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lufHeNbIKP6lddX37Sf8h",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10573.466720695013,
      "y": 393.154415109261,
      "width": 809.208144823815,
      "height": 45.49999999999994,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1707771024,
      "version": 2723,
      "versionNonce": 1658579568,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788458185660,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Microtasks have higher priority than Tasks.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Microtasks have higher priority than Tasks.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7i_cQ861HR1FumUu1auAm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11056.800054028346,
      "y": 906.4877484425942,
      "width": 869.208144823815,
      "height": 45.49999999999994,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1193742960,
      "version": 2964,
      "versionNonce": 1371555936,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "SvjIBcvj4P5hIEaKOiqPE",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1788536519433,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In this example the output will be A D C and B",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In this example the output will be A D C and B",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "SDMiaXzNApy2UE-aZ_qpb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12370.13338736168,
      "y": 741.154415109261,
      "width": 1717.5414781571465,
      "height": 591.4999999999993,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1519181936,
      "version": 3203,
      "versionNonce": 1305587808,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "SvjIBcvj4P5hIEaKOiqPE",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1788536519434,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Task is basically work that the browser schedules to run later, such as callbacks from:\n\nsetTimeout()\nsetInterval()\nDOM events\n\nand get store at the task queue and called by the event loop if the stack is empty\n\nQ.) Suppose we have 100s or 1000s of lines of code then the Task will run after the 100 lines ?\nthe callback can run before those 100 lines finish, but only if the Call Stack becomes empty.\nThe key thing is: JavaScript does not normally become empty in the middle of one continuous\nsynchronous execution. so if we have 100 lines of syncronous code and we have a timeout at line\nsecond the the timeout callback will NOT interrupt those 100 synchronous lines.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A Task is basically work that the browser schedules to run later, such as callbacks from:\n\nsetTimeout()\nsetInterval()\nDOM events\n\nand get store at the task queue and called by the event loop if the stack is empty\n\nQ.) Suppose we have 100s or 1000s of lines of code then the Task will run after the 100 lines ?\nthe callback can run before those 100 lines finish, but only if the Call Stack becomes empty.\nThe key thing is: JavaScript does not normally become empty in the middle of one continuous synchronous execution. so if we have 100 lines of syncronous code and we have a timeout at line second the the timeout callback will NOT interrupt those 100 synchronous lines.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "unJWXpiVxPigB2llxRv_K",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12373.466720695013,
      "y": -767.8455848907388,
      "width": 1717.5414781571465,
      "height": 90.99999999999989,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1309545072,
      "version": 3826,
      "versionNonce": 1883669920,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788536516954,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now We have two ways to handle promise async/await and .then() .catch() and promise look like\nthis const promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {}); and it itself is not asynronous for e.g.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now We have two ways to handle promise async/await and .then() .catch() and promise look like this const promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {}); and it itself is not asynronous for e.g.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "AvtiSvwN1cI0vr7iyVBLN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12385.966720695013,
      "y": -1455.3455848907388,
      "width": 1717.5414781571465,
      "height": 90.99999999999989,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bt8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2147125904,
      "version": 4015,
      "versionNonce": 1554305440,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788536516954,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Don't run this callback before 0ms; once the timer is eligible, put its callback into the task\nqueue, and it can run when the current JavaScript task is finished.\"",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Don't run this callback before 0ms; once the timer is eligible, put its callback into the task queue, and it can run when the current JavaScript task is finished.\"",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "gDPxIUrkOQn1-b-aLnPXi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12365.966720695013,
      "y": -1999.3455848907388,
      "width": 1371.5414781571476,
      "height": 272.99999999999966,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 971694224,
      "version": 4254,
      "versionNonce": 1993560160,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1788536519436,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "It lets you directly put a callback into the Microtask Queue.\n\nWhy do we need queueMicrotask()?\n\nSometimes you want something to execute after the current synchronous\ncode finishes, but before the next task/timer.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "It lets you directly put a callback into the Microtask Queue.\n\nWhy do we need queueMicrotask()?\n\nSometimes you want something to execute after the current synchronous code finishes, but before the next task/timer.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "bGjevaZN4W0qAZ2F4mhPr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19190.13338736168,
      "y": -2983.1821888964655,
      "width": 1036.5414781571476,
      "height": 181.99999999999977,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btAV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 390582746,
      "version": 4795,
      "versionNonce": 579216366,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790151402230,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every property in object have a property descriptor.\nwhich we can inspect using this\nObject.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(person, \"name\"); and get\nthe output we see in image",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every property in object have a property descriptor.\nwhich we can inspect using this Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(person, \"name\"); and get the output we see in image",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
