      "updated": 1790160997530,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When we send data over TCP as a stream, TCP guarantees that the bytes arrive in the correct order, but it\ndoes not guarantee how those bytes will be split into chunks when we receive them. For example, if we send 100\nbytes, we might receive them as 30 + 20 + 50 bytes or in some other chunk sizes. So we keep collecting the\nincoming chunks in a buffer until we have enough bytes to form a complete message according to our application\nprotocol, and then we interpret those bytes using something like a TypedArray or DataView",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When we send data over TCP as a stream, TCP guarantees that the bytes arrive in the correct order, but it does not guarantee how those bytes will be split into chunks when we receive them. For example, if we send 100 bytes, we might receive them as 30 + 20 + 50 bytes or in some other chunk sizes. So we keep collecting the incoming chunks in a buffer until we have enough bytes to form a complete message according to our application protocol, and then we interpret those bytes using something like a TypedArray or DataView",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
