      "updated": 1790151390880,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now when we create object from the function directly then remeber \"new\" keyword creates a new\nobject.\n\nPerson act as a constructor when it is simply invoked with \"new\" keyword (e.g., new Person(...)),\nwhich creates a new object. every regular function is created with a .prototype object ( remeber\nclasses also have this property as they are also functions ) and every methods are get into the\n\".prototype\" and it is connected to the \"first [[prototype]]\". when you do Person.prototype.greet\n= function(){} person object get a [[prototype]] in which it has a greet function and in the\n[[prototype]] it has a more [[prototype]] which have (toString , valueOf .. etc)\n\nthis.name and this.age refers to the new object you are creating so when you do p = new\nPerson(\"shivam\" , 21) it will look like this obj = {name : shivam , age : 21 } and the function greet()\nwill goes to the [[prototype]] of the object you have createted.",
      "fontSize": 35.5947838679886,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now when we create object from the function directly then remeber \"new\" keyword creates a new object.\n\nPerson act as a constructor when it is simply invoked with \"new\" keyword (e.g., new Person(...)), which creates a new object. every regular function is created with a .prototype object ( remeber classes also have this property as they are also functions ) and every methods are get into the \".prototype\" and it is connected to the \"first [[prototype]]\". when you do Person.prototype.greet = function(){} person object get a [[prototype]] in which it has a greet function and in the [[prototype]] it has a more [[prototype]] which have (toString , valueOf .. etc)\n\nthis.name and this.age refers to the new object you are creating so when you do p = new Person(\"shivam\" , 21) it will look like this obj = {name : shivam , age : 21 } and the function greet() will goes to the [[prototype]] of the object you have createted.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
