    {
      "id": "HqvfMc2LcgOfJXaQfdI6C",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 14386.323863552156,
      "y": -2467.2792394598987,
      "width": 1531.0414781571492,
      "height": 727.9999999999991,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btBV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 55824480,
      "version": 5628,
      "versionNonce": 198494624,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788539711517,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Rendering / Painting is a separate than a javascript execution call stack\n\nCurrent JS task finishes → microtasks finish → browser gets a rendering opportunity\n→ then it paints.\n\ndocument.body.style.background = \"red\" is NOT an async task, so it does not go into\nthe Microtask Queue.\nNow suppose we have a script in which we have :- \n\nbox.style.background = \"red\";\nbox.style.background = \"blue\";\nbox.style.background = \"green\";\n\nJavaScript simply changes the style state :- background = red -> background = blue ->\nbackground = green but render the ui at the screen when js execution is done thats it\nbecome effecient and also skip the frames ",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Rendering / Painting is a separate than a javascript execution call stack\n\nCurrent JS task finishes → microtasks finish → browser gets a rendering opportunity → then it paints.\n\ndocument.body.style.background = \"red\" is NOT an async task, so it does not go into the Microtask Queue.\nNow suppose we have a script in which we have :- \n\nbox.style.background = \"red\";\nbox.style.background = \"blue\";\nbox.style.background = \"green\";\n\nJavaScript simply changes the style state :- background = red -> background = blue -> background = green but render the ui at the screen when js execution is done thats it become effecient and also skip the frames ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "eOh81l1i0WEiwZ63UukX1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 14382.323863552156,
      "y": -1464.1850831140368,
      "width": 1531.0414781571492,
      "height": 500.4999999999994,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btBl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 941943200,
      "version": 5739,
      "versionNonce": 1435843680,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788541496463,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "when we write requestAnimationFrame(() => {box.style.left = \"100px\";});\n\nyou're saying: \"Browser, call this callback before the next rendering opportunity.\"\n\nNow suppose we have code :- \n\nfunction animate() {\n    box.style.left = \"100px\";\n    requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n}\nanimate(); ",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "when we write requestAnimationFrame(() => {box.style.left = \"100px\";});\n\nyou're saying: \"Browser, call this callback before the next rendering opportunity.\"\n\nNow suppose we have code :- \n\nfunction animate() {\n    box.style.left = \"100px\";\n    requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n}\nanimate(); ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Yj_dtgNyy2N2j9879WF4e",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 14378.903180746158,
      "y": -949.950857688745,
      "width": 2035.2757035824434,
      "height": 909.9999999999989,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btBt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1034279008,
      "version": 6314,
      "versionNonce": 440569248,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788541845416,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now How this code works and the flow and this is also a infinite recurion why this do not get freeze ? \n\nThe Frame Begins:The browser takes your animate callback out of the queue and puts it on the call stack. \nYour Function Runs: - box.style.left = \"100px\" runs (goes to call stack). JavaScript marks the element as \"needs a\nnew style/layout.\"\n- requestAnimationFrame(animate) runs. It drops a ticket for animate into the queue for the next frame.animate\nfinishes and leaves the call stack.\n\nNow that the call stack is empty:The browser calculates the new position of box (left: 100px). It paints the\nscreen once.\n\nNow why it do not get freeze ?\nThe browser does not immediately grab that next callback from the queue.\nIt pauses and lets the screen rest until the monitor's next hardware refresh tick (about 16 milliseconds later on a\n60Hz display).\nBecause it pauses between each paint, the browser has plenty of time to handle clicks, scrolling, and user input.\nThat is why the page stays completely smooth and never freezes.\n\n|--- Run rAF (e.g. 2ms) ---|--- Style & Paint (e.g. 3ms) ---|--- Free time for Clicks / Input (11ms) ---|\n<------------------------------------ Total Frame: ~16.6ms ------------------------------------>",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now How this code works and the flow and this is also a infinite recurion why this do not get freeze ? \n\nThe Frame Begins:The browser takes your animate callback out of the queue and puts it on the call stack. \nYour Function Runs: - box.style.left = \"100px\" runs (goes to call stack). JavaScript marks the element as \"needs a new style/layout.\"\n- requestAnimationFrame(animate) runs. It drops a ticket for animate into the queue for the next frame.animate finishes and leaves the call stack.\n\nNow that the call stack is empty:The browser calculates the new position of box (left: 100px). It paints the screen once.\n\nNow why it do not get freeze ?\nThe browser does not immediately grab that next callback from the queue.\nIt pauses and lets the screen rest until the monitor's next hardware refresh tick (about 16 milliseconds later on a 60Hz display).\nBecause it pauses between each paint, the browser has plenty of time to handle clicks, scrolling, and user input. That is why the page stays completely smooth and never freezes.\n\n|--- Run rAF (e.g. 2ms) ---|--- Style & Paint (e.g. 3ms) ---|--- Free time for Clicks / Input (11ms) ---|\n<------------------------------------ Total Frame: ~16.6ms ------------------------------------>",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "L5FrV8AQtaDf5HOWqZ1bn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12390.966720695013,
      "y": -1337.8455848907388,
