      "updated": 1788536516954,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here the output will be A after C and B now see when we print A\nawait is a async task which get processed and send to the queue\nuntil that JS continue execution so it rake log(\"after\"). then call\nstack become emty then print C and B. so it makes the function\nsyncronuous but at global level it is asyncronuous \nAnd remember a async function always return a Promise",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here the output will be A after C and B now see when we print A await is a async task which get processed and send to the queue until that JS continue execution so it rake log(\"after\"). then call stack become emty then print C and B. so it makes the function syncronuous but at global level it is asyncronuous \nAnd remember a async function always return a Promise",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "MGFnpPTc58hrwfvbpLWem",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12371.466720695013,
      "y": -663.8455848907388,
      "width": 1717.5414781571465,
      "height": 272.99999999999966,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bu",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 495941744,
      "version": 4252,
      "versionNonce": 595794336,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788536516954,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Asyncronous items are send to the queue thats why we say these are runs at the background\nwhen we use async await, at the browser level it waits until the promise get fullfiled or reject \nthen it send it to the miscrotask queue then event loop take it and send to the call stack then\nwe see the result\nNow asyn await create the function syncronous where we apply it but at the global level it is\nworks asyncronously for e.g.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Asyncronous items are send to the queue thats why we say these are runs at the background when we use async await, at the browser level it waits until the promise get fullfiled or reject \nthen it send it to the miscrotask queue then event loop take it and send to the call stack then we see the result\nNow asyn await create the function syncronous where we apply it but at the global level it is works asyncronously for e.g.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "K-XJOKQTlY86gKcEQMlVy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12373.466720695013,
      "y": -13.845584890738792,
      "width": 1181.5414781571465,
      "height": 227.49999999999972,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bx",
